```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Archive Utility Invoked on Sensitive Directory (Staging for Exfil)
# Detection ID: DE-CO-001
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1560.001 - Archive Collected Data: Archive via Utility
# Data Source: Sysmon EventCode=1
# Severity: Medium
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
Image IN ("*\\7z.exe","*\\WinRAR.exe","*\\rar.exe","*\\tar.exe")
CommandLine IN ("*\\Finance*","*\\HR*","*\\Legal*","*password*","*-p*")
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(CommandLine) as cmd by ComputerName, User, Image
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
```

## Detection Logic
Archive tools invoked against sensitive business-unit directories, especially with a password flag (common to evade DLP content inspection), indicate an attacker staging data for exfiltration.

## False Positive Considerations
IT staff performing legitimate backups or migrations. Restrict/tune the directory name list to your actual crown-jewel data locations and coordinate with data owners.

## Tuning Notes
Extend to flag archive file sizes >100MB written to temp/user-writable directories via FileCreate (EventCode 11) correlation for higher fidelity.
